==German==

===Etymology===
Originally called {{etyl|en|de}} ''[[cake]]s'' by Hermann Bahlsen, who brought the idea to Germany in 1889. From 1911 his company changed the name of the article to ''Keks''; at the time, the plural was also ''Keks''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/keːks/|lang=de}}

===Noun===
'''Keks''' {{g|m}} or {{g|n}} (''plural'' '''[[Kekse]]''')

# A [[cookie]].

